      "en": "# Find Animation Opportunities\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Domain:** `DESIGN` | **Source:** `emilkowalski/skills` | **License:** `UNLICENSED` | **Installs:** `230,805`\n\n## ⚡ Overview & Capabilities\nSearch a codebase or UI for places that don't animate but should, and reject everything that shouldn't. Read-only; it proposes motion with exact values, it does not implement it. Use when the user asks \"what could be animated here?\" or wants to \"make this feel more alive\". For fixing existing animations, use improve-animations or review-animations instead.\n\nThis skill delivers production-verified operational rules, architecture constraints, and executable guidelines directly integrated into your agent execution loop.\n\n## 🎯 Primary Use Cases\n- When implementing, debugging, or reviewing workflows related to **Find Animation Opportunities**.\n- Enforcing domain best practices and eliminating hallucinated parameters.\n- Executing standard terminal and API actions via `npx skills add emilkowalski/skills --skill find-animation-opportunities`.\n\n## 🛠️ Verification & Safety\n- **Supply Chain Safety:** Verified safe from supply-chain injection, telemetry leakage, and malicious dependencies.\n- **Agent Interoperability:** Compatible with all standard AI agent platforms including Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, and Gemini CLI.\n",
