      "en": "# Animate Expo\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Domain:** `DESIGN` | **Source:** `emilkowalski/skills` | **License:** `UNLICENSED` | **Installs:** `157,822`\n\n## ⚡ Overview & Capabilities\nBuild animations in React Native and Expo, making the decisions in the order that determines whether they feel right — should it animate, which thread it runs on, which properties, spring or timing, how the gesture hands off, how it degrades. Writes the implementation with Reanimated, Gesture Handler, Expo Router and expo-haptics. Use when animating anything in an Expo app, adding gestures, sheets, screen transitions, press feedback or haptics, or fixing motion that stutters on device. For web animation use `animate`.\n\nThis skill delivers production-verified operational rules, architecture constraints, and executable guidelines directly integrated into your agent execution loop.\n\n## 🎯 Primary Use Cases\n- When implementing, debugging, or reviewing workflows related to **Animate Expo**.\n- Enforcing domain best practices and eliminating hallucinated parameters.\n- Executing standard terminal and API actions via `npx skills add emilkowalski/skills --skill animate-expo`.\n\n## 🛠️ Verification & Safety\n- **Supply Chain Safety:** Verified safe from supply-chain injection, telemetry leakage, and malicious dependencies.\n- **Agent Interoperability:** Compatible with all standard AI agent platforms including Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, and Gemini CLI.\n",
