      "en": "# Directory Submissions\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Domain:** `MARKETING` | **Source:** `coreyhaines31/marketingskills` | **License:** `UNLICENSED` | **Installs:** `90,570`\n\n## ⚡ Overview & Capabilities\nWhen the user wants to submit their product to startup, SaaS, AI, agent, MCP, no-code, or review directories for backlinks, domain rating, and discovery. Also use when the user mentions \"directory submissions,\" \"submit to directories,\" \"backlinks from directories,\" \"list my product,\" \"submit to Product Hunt,\" \"BetaList,\" \"TAAFT,\" \"Futurepedia,\" \"G2 listing,\" \"Capterra listing,\" \"AlternativeTo,\" \"SaaSHub,\" \"AI directories,\" \"MCP registry,\" \"publish my MCP server,\" \"awesome list,\" \"llms.txt directory,\" \"Claude plugin directory,\" \"agent directory,\" \"dofollow backlinks,\" \"launch directories,\" or \"directory tracker.\" Use this whenever someone is planning the directory layer of a product launch or an ongoing backlink campaign. For the broader launch moment, see launch. For programmatic SEO pages that should live behind these backlinks, see programmatic-seo. For AI citation optimization, see ai-seo.\n\nThis skill delivers production-verified operational rules, architecture constraints, and executable guidelines directly integrated into your agent execution loop.\n\n## 🎯 Primary Use Cases\n- When implementing, debugging, or reviewing workflows related to **Directory Submissions**.\n- Enforcing domain best practices and eliminating hallucinated parameters.\n- Executing standard terminal and API actions via `npx skills add coreyhaines31/marketingskills --skill directory-submissions`.\n\n## 🛠️ Verification & Safety\n- **Supply Chain Safety:** Verified safe from supply-chain injection, telemetry leakage, and malicious dependencies.\n- **Agent Interoperability:** Compatible with all standard AI agent platforms including Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, and Gemini CLI.\n",
