      "en": "# Security And Hardening\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Domain:** `CODING` | **Source:** `addyosmani/agent-skills` | **License:** `MIT` | **Installs:** `77,660`\n\n## ⚡ Overview & Capabilities\nHardens code against vulnerabilities. Use when auditing an input handler for vulnerabilities, when handling user input, authentication, data storage, or external integrations, or when checking a login flow is safe against the OWASP Top Ten. Use when building any feature that accepts untrusted data, manages user sessions or session cookies, or interacts with third-party services. Use when auditing dependencies for known vulnerabilities, triaging package-manager audit findings, or assessing supply-chain risk in a new package. Use when personal data or privacy compliance (GDPR, CCPA) is involved.\n\nThis skill delivers production-verified operational rules, architecture constraints, and executable guidelines directly integrated into your agent execution loop.\n\n## 🎯 Primary Use Cases\n- When implementing, debugging, or reviewing workflows related to **Security And Hardening**.\n- Enforcing domain best practices and eliminating hallucinated parameters.\n- Executing standard terminal and API actions via `npx skills add addyosmani/agent-skills --skill security-and-hardening`.\n\n## 🛠️ Verification & Safety\n- **Supply Chain Safety:** Verified safe from supply-chain injection, telemetry leakage, and malicious dependencies.\n- **Agent Interoperability:** Compatible with all standard AI agent platforms including Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, and Gemini CLI.\n",
