      "en": "# GIT Commit\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Domain:** `CODING` | **Source:** `github/awesome-copilot` | **License:** `MIT` | **Installs:** `48,023`\n\n## ⚡ Overview & Capabilities\nUse this skill when the user wants to make a Git commit or split changes into more than one commit. Also use it when the user types \"/commit\" or asks for a conventional commit. The skill examines the diff, stages the related files, writes a Conventional Commits message, and runs git commit. Do not use it when the user wants only a commit message and no commit. Do not use it to push, open a pull request, rebase, or change the commit history.\n\nThis skill delivers production-verified operational rules, architecture constraints, and executable guidelines directly integrated into your agent execution loop.\n\n## 🎯 Primary Use Cases\n- When implementing, debugging, or reviewing workflows related to **GIT Commit**.\n- Enforcing domain best practices and eliminating hallucinated parameters.\n- Executing standard terminal and API actions via `npx skills add github/awesome-copilot --skill git-commit`.\n\n## 🛠️ Verification & Safety\n- **Supply Chain Safety:** Verified safe from supply-chain injection, telemetry leakage, and malicious dependencies.\n- **Agent Interoperability:** Compatible with all standard AI agent platforms including Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, and Gemini CLI.\n",
