      "en": "# Limrun Bazel\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Domain:** `MOBILE` | **Source:** `limrun-inc/skills` | **License:** `UNLICENSED` | **Installs:** `27,435`\n\n## ⚡ Overview & Capabilities\nThe default way to build any Bazel workspace on Limrun: build its iOS and Android targets on Limrun's shared build plane with `lim bazel setup` and `bazel build --config=limrun`, from any environment (Linux, Windows, macOS, VM, container, CI), with one remote cache shared across the organization. Use when the project is a Bazel workspace (MODULE.bazel) with rules_apple or rules_android and the user wants to build it remotely, run the built app on a Limrun simulator or emulator, set up Bazel remote execution in CI, or fix a `--config=limrun` build that fails on authentication, workers, or missing MODULE.bazel lines. limrun-xcode-bazel covers only the legacy `lim xcode rbe` flow; use it only when the workspace already runs on `lim xcode rbe` or the user asks for it. For non-Bazel Android builds, use limrun-gradle.\n\nThis skill delivers production-verified operational rules, architecture constraints, and executable guidelines directly integrated into your agent execution loop.\n\n## 🎯 Primary Use Cases\n- When implementing, debugging, or reviewing workflows related to **Limrun Bazel**.\n- Enforcing domain best practices and eliminating hallucinated parameters.\n- Executing standard terminal and API actions via `npx skills add limrun-inc/skills --skill limrun-bazel`.\n\n## 🛠️ Verification & Safety\n- **Supply Chain Safety:** Verified safe from supply-chain injection, telemetry leakage, and malicious dependencies.\n- **Agent Interoperability:** Compatible with all standard AI agent platforms including Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, and Gemini CLI.\n",
